<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Privacy Policy — Evo Meals' }) %>
<meta name="description" content="How Evo Meals collects, uses, shares, and retains data from parents, students, schools, and catering partners.">
</head>
<body>

<%- include('partials/sitenav', { active: '' }) %>

<section class="hero hero-inner-page">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="hero-copy" data-reveal style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated 1 June 2026. This explains what we collect, why, who it's shared with, and how long we keep it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap legal-content">

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Evo Meals collects different information depending on how you use the platform:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Parents and students</strong> — account details (name, email, phone), each student's Civil ID (used solely to verify identity at tap-to-collect and prevent meal collection by the wrong student), allergy and dietary information you provide for each student, and payment activity (bookings, charges, refunds — we do not store full card numbers).</li>
      <li><strong>Schools</strong> — the school name associated with each student, and, for school administrators, an account login and the meal-program activity for their own school.</li>
      <li><strong>Schools and caterers making a partnership inquiry</strong> — the organization name, the name and role of the contact person, and any scale, arrangement, or message details submitted through our inquiry forms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To operate the core service — bookings, tap-to-collect verification, subscription charges, and dashboard reporting for parents and school administrators.</li>
      <li>To keep students safe — allergy information is shown to catering and serving staff at the point of preparation and collection, and nowhere else.</li>
      <li>To respond to partnership inquiries from schools and caterers.</li>
      <li>To maintain the security of accounts, including detecting unusual login activity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's shared with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data. Information is shared only as needed to run the service:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The parent's name, the student's information (name, class, school, allergy and dietary notes), and the school's information are shared with our independent catering partner specifically to fulfill meal preparation and delivery — Evo Meals does not prepare food itself.</li>
      <li>A student's allergy information and meal selection are visible to the catering partner preparing that student's meals, and to the student's own school administrator for their school's program.</li>
      <li>A school administrator sees program-level data (subscriptions, meal counts, activity) for their own school only — never data belonging to another school.</li>
      <li>Partnership inquiry details are used internally to follow up with the submitting organization and are not shared with third parties.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Allergen and dietary information</h2>
    <p>Special dietary claims on a dish — nut-free, shellfish-free, sesame-free, soy-free, egg-free, gluten-free, lactose-free — apply to that specific preparation, are not a blanket guarantee across every dish, and are not independently verified by Evo Meals. Please use your own judgment for a child with a specific allergy.</p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>Account and booking data is kept for as long as an account remains active, plus a limited period afterward for financial record-keeping (charge and refund history). Partnership inquiries are retained until the inquiry is resolved or the submitting organization asks us to remove it. You can request deletion of your account data at any time using the contact path below.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can review and update a student's allergy information at any time from your dashboard. You can request a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it, by contacting us using the details below.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy, or requests regarding your data, can be sent through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, or by email to <strong>privacy@evomeals.example</strong>.</p>

  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/sitefoot') %>

</body>
</html>
